{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "01a08154-4c27-7551-9cfa-e8e7d2bcf73a", "turn_id": "01a12792-c760-7722-98c3-520e7ab1df8a", "item_id": "exec-db3097d5-8245-4386-9a93-28807074acc0", "rollout_ordinal": 2423, "created_at_ms": 1791665302189, "item_type": "webSearch", "updated_at_ordinal": 2423, "started_at_ms": 1791665302189, "completed_at_ms": 1791665304930}, "item": {"type": "webSearch", "id": "exec-db3097d5-8245-4386-9a93-28807074acc0", "query": "OpenAI Responses API structured outputs ...", "action": {"type": "search", "query": null, "queries": ["OpenAI Responses API structured outputs", "Ollama structured outputs API", "Gemini API structured outputs"]}, "results": [{"type": "text_result", "domain": "developers.openai.com", "ref_id": "turn11search0", "snippet": "Structured Outputs is available in two forms in the OpenAI API: ... * If you are connecting the model to tools, functions, data, etc. in", "title": "Structured model outputs | OpenAI API", "url": "https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/structured-outputs?api-mode=responses"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "developers.openai.com", "ref_id": "turn11search1", "snippet": "Configuring `{ \"type\": \"json_schema\" }` enables Structured Outputs, which ensures the model will match your supplied JSON schema. ... content: array of ResponseOutputText { annotations,", "title": "Create a model response | OpenAI API Reference", "url": "https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/resources/responses/methods/create"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "developers.openai.com", "ref_id": "turn11search2", "snippet": "An object specifying the format that the model must output.Configuring `{ \"type\": \"json_schema\" }` enables Structured Outputs, which ensures the model will match your supplied", "title": "Responses | OpenAI API Reference", "url": "https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/python/resources/responses"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "developers.openai.com", "ref_id": "turn11search3", "snippet": "An object specifying the format that the model must output.Configuring `{ \"type\": \"json_schema\" }` enables Structured Outputs, which ensures the model will match your supplied", "title": "Get a model response | OpenAI API Reference", "url": "https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/resources/responses/methods/retrieve"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "ai.google.dev", "ref_id": "turn11search4", "snippet": "model=\"gemini-3.8-flash\", ... To learn how to define more complex structures and recursive schemas, see the structured output guide.", "title": "Getting started  |  Gemini API  |  Google AI for Developers", "url": "https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/get-started"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "developers.openai.com", "ref_id": "turn11search5", "snippet": "Structured Outputs is available in two forms in the OpenAI API: ... * If you are connecting the model to tools, functions, data, etc. in", "title": "Structured model outputs | OpenAI API", "url": "https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/structured-outputs?api-mode=responses&trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_little-text-block"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "developers.openai.com", "ref_id": "turn11search6", "snippet": "With the OpenAI API, you can use a large language model to generate text from a prompt, as you might using ChatGPT.Models can generate almost", "title": "Text generation | OpenAI API", "url": "https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/text"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "developers.openai.com", "ref_id": "turn11search7", "snippet": "Structured Outputs can be enabled by setting the parameter `strict: true` in an API call with either a defined response format or function definitions. ...", "title": "Introduction to Structured Outputs", "url": "https://developers.openai.com/cookbook/examples/structured_outputs_intro"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "ai.google.dev", "ref_id": "turn11search8", "snippet": "In addition to supporting JSON Schema in the REST API, the Google GenAI SDKs allow defining schemas using Pydantic (Python) and Zod (JavaScript). ... You", "title": "Structured outputs  |  Gemini API  |  Google AI for Developers", "url": "https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/structured-output?authuser=683989221"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "ai.google.dev", "ref_id": "turn11search9", "snippet": "Gemini offers two methods for generating structured outputs.", "title": "Using tools with Gemini API  |  Google AI for Developers", "url": "https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/tools.md"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "ai.google.dev", "ref_id": "turn11search10", "snippet": "Gemini 3 lets you combine Structured Outputs with built-in tools, including Grounding with Google Search, URL Context, Code Execution, File Search, and Function Calling. ...", "title": "Structured outputs  |  Gemini Generate Content API (Legacy)  |  Google AI for Developers", "url": "https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/generate-content/structured-output?hl=en"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "developers.openai.com", "ref_id": "turn11search11", "snippet": "Structured Outputs schemas and function schemas are themselves JSON objects, so we leverage Structured Outputs to generate them. ... For structured output schemas, wrap them", "title": "Prompt generation | OpenAI API", "url": "https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/prompt-generation"}]}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "01a08154-4c27-7551-9cfa-e8e7d2bcf73a", "turn_id": "01a12792-c760-7722-98c3-520e7ab1df8a", "item_id": "exec-55ab16fd-4d8e-4cb3-bc0e-40e203cd1497", "rollout_ordinal": 2428, "created_at_ms": 1791665307734, "item_type": "webSearch", "updated_at_ordinal": 2428, "started_at_ms": 1791665307734, "completed_at_ms": 1791665310012}, "item": {"type": "webSearch", "id": "exec-55ab16fd-4d8e-4cb3-bc0e-40e203cd1497", "query": "https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/structured-outputs", "action": {"type": "openPage", "url": "https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/structured-outputs"}, "results": [{"type": "text_result", "domain": "developers.openai.com", "ref_id": "turn12view0", "snippet": "Total lines: 18032", "thumbnail_url": "https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-1/rh1Ew2qZw_vqg80ljqvwuH-kX6W3XERImsld50vNrRAvIREmZiWaJwTTy3AawW2bRUQnP65ZIf8nfQiSMH0aFIbLCwRvy01wsTIbX1sGOWqQJna1b34F1yOtXtZkXNXY", "title": "Structured model outputs | OpenAI API", "url": "https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/structured-outputs"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "docs.ollama.com", "ref_id": "turn12view1", "snippet": "Total lines: 213", "title": "Structured Outputs - Ollama", "url": "https://docs.ollama.com/capabilities/structured-outputs"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "ai.google.dev", "ref_id": "turn12view2", "snippet": "Total lines: 1609", "thumbnail_url": "https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-1/gFYER7ui4vmNPOuMwMAP72kijuSAL2l2eri-Tok4ZpuiI1uq2ovYVgn5Rp8DH04YCZ4qxvikWBXduwZqoawRuEyXqdwR2BPjaDqSUdOlhjiUYhUVnDijikRlWFGIhmai", "title": "Structured outputs  |  Gemini API  |  Google AI for Developers", "url": "https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/structured-output"}]}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "01a08154-4c27-7551-9cfa-e8e7d2bcf73a", "turn_id": "01a12792-c760-7722-98c3-520e7ab1df8a", "item_id": "msg_06f6aa8593d2a892016acaa4a0c50c87d28aa6ddfcc4f2c07a", "rollout_ordinal": 2431, "created_at_ms": 1791665311879, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2431, "started_at_ms": 1791665311879, "completed_at_ms": 1791665323150}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "msg_06f6aa8593d2a892016acaa4a0c50c87d28aa6ddfcc4f2c07a", "text": "**Lo conectaría como una capa de redacción sobre nuestro análisis.** El backend calcula las métricas y detecta los eventos; el LLM recibe esos resultados y los explica en español. Para esta primera versión no necesitamos enviarle audio ni entrenar un modelo.\n\nTenemos estas opciones:\n\n| Opción | Ventaja | Consideración |\n|---|---|---|\n| **OpenAI mediante API** | Permite pedir una respuesta con estructura fija para mostrarla en la app. | Requiere conexión y acceso a la API. |\n| **Gemini mediante API** | También admite respuestas estructuradas; sería una alternativa intercambiable. | Requiere conexión y acceso al servicio. |\n| **Modelo local con Ollama** | Podemos ejecutar la generación en tu computador. | La velocidad y calidad dependerán del modelo y del hardware. |\n\nLas tres opciones permiten solicitar respuestas siguiendo un esquema JSON. Esto facilita separar resumen, aciertos y recomendaciones, aunque **un formato correcto no garantiza que la explicación sea fiel a los datos**. Documentación: [OpenAI](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/structured-outputs), [Gemini](https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/structured-output) y [Ollama](https://docs.ollama.com/capabilities/structured-outputs).\n\n**Por el tiempo disponible, empezaría con una API**, dejando el proveedor configurable. La integración sería:\n\n1. **Termina la grabación:** nuestro backend produce el análisis por fragmentos.\n2. **Prepara el contexto:** enviamos métricas, eventos, tiempos e instrucciones de interpretación.\n3. **El modelo redacta:** devuelve un resumen y, por fragmento, aciertos, aspectos a revisar y práctica sugerida.\n4. **El backend valida:** comprueba el formato, los IDs de evidencia y que correspondan al fragmento correcto. La fidelidad del texto también se evalúa con casos de prueba.\n5. **Guardamos la explicación:** ambas interfaces pueden mostrarla sin volver a consultar al modelo cada vez.\n\nGeneraría **un resumen inicial y el detalle de cada fragmento cuando el usuario lo abra**, guardando cada respuesta. Así evitamos generar de entrada 36 explicaciones para Reik.\n\nSi la consulta falla, la app seguiría mostrando las métricas y una explicación básica mediante plantillas.\n\nMi propuesta concreta es **OpenAI como primera conexión, un módulo independiente para poder cambiar de proveedor y respuestas estructuradas con referencias a nuestra evidencia**. No necesitamos agentes, búsquedas externas ni entrenamiento adicional para esta etapa.", "phase": "final_answer", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "01a08154-4c27-7551-9cfa-e8e7d2bcf73a", "turn_id": "01a12794-bcaa-7830-9c20-3c3ab3739e8f", "item_id": "01a12794-bd36-7fb0-af5e-931e572e93c4", "rollout_ordinal": 2440, "created_at_ms": 1791665421642, "item_type": "userMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2440, "started_at_ms": 1791665421642, "completed_at_ms": 1791665421642}, "item": {"type": "userMessage", "id": "01a12794-bd36-7fb0-af5e-931e572e93c4", "clientId": "6f82ff00-0e19-4df1-b5f2-860f3f5fb81c", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "hazlo como propones, haz tambien la interfaz grafica necesaria para mostrar los resultados, despues la ajustamos\n", "text_elements": []}]}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "01a08154-4c27-7551-9cfa-e8e7d2bcf73a", "turn_id": "01a12794-bcaa-7830-9c20-3c3ab3739e8f", "item_id": "msg_06f6aa8593d2a892016acaa510845087d2b384d59e07f4b497", "rollout_ordinal": 2441, "created_at_ms": 1791665423705, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2441, "started_at_ms": 1791665423705, "completed_at_ms": 1791665424693}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "msg_06f6aa8593d2a892016acaa510845087d2b384d59e07f4b497", "text": "Voy a conectar la generación de explicaciones y añadir una primera interfaz para el resumen y los fragmentos. La app podrá mostrar resultados básicos aunque la API no esté configurada, y guardará las explicaciones generadas para reutilizarlas.\n", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
